## Context

The 2026-09-28 LAIR run on clean main (267ab6bb) ran `make check` outside the
Codex sandbox. The full suite finished with 1 failure and 1,113 passes:
`tests/test_resident_census.py::test_channel_budgets` measured 7,291 characters
of resident skill names and descriptions against the 7,000-character cap. This
is a standing CI gate, not a flaky runtime probe. The sandbox run had unrelated
`BASH_ENV` startup failures; its failing test passed outside the sandbox.

## Action

Trim skill descriptions while preserving the cues needed to select each skill.
Regenerate the README skills catalog and inspect the changed descriptions as a
set; keep the existing budget rather than raising it to absorb drift.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Resident skill descriptions total at most 7,000 characters.
- [ ] The README skills catalog is in sync with the descriptions.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
